## The Year in Recalls: By the Numbers

337 recalls have been issued so far this year, and among them, 91 have been classified as Class I, indicating a serious health risk. While we're still on track to possibly beat last year's numbers, it's the nature of these recalls that deserves attention--particularly the presence of unapproved additives and undeclared allergens.

## Spotting the Colors of Concern

Unapproved colorants, such as FD&amp;C Yellow 5, Yellow 6, and Red 40, have prominently appeared in our most recent recalls. Notably, Guangdong Zonegoing Food Co., LTD had multiple recalls for their 52USA brand Popping Boba products containing these unapproved additives. On top of that, the lack of proper labeling for allergens in products like Einstein Bros Bagels Cream Cheese by Schreiber Foods Inc is another alarming issue.

## Foreign Objects in Unlikely Places

Glass pieces in Lactalis Canada, Inc.'s Vanilla Creme Brulee? This alarming oversight serves as a clear reminder of why we need stringent quality control measures across the food industry.

## The Repeat Offender Problem

It's also disconcerting to note that 68 of this year's recalls involve parties with a history of previous incidents. Moonlight Packing Corporation and Albertsons Companies LLC continue to receive failing grades for multiple Class I recalls in just the first half of 2026.

## Closing Thoughts

While we can't control what happens in production facilities, we can control what we bring into our homes. By staying informed, we empower ourselves to make safer choices.
